-orchestrator","data-pipelines","data-science","elt","etl","machine-learning","mlops","orchestration","python","scheduler","workflow","workflow-engine","workflow-orchestration"],"visibility":"public","forks":18214,"open_issues":1927,"watchers":47308,"default_branch":"main","permissions":{"admin":false,"maintain":false,"push":false,"triage":false,"pull":true}},"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/airflow/pulls/66911","html_url":"https://github.com/apache/airflow/pull/66911","diff_url":"https://github.com/apache/airflow/pull/66911.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/apache/airflow/pull/66911.patch","merged_at":null},"body":"`DagRunOperations.trigger()` sent `POST /execution/dag-runs/{dag_id}/{run_id}` through the generic execution API retry layer. That POST is not idempotent. If the server created the Dag run but the client lost the response, the retry POSTed the same run ID again and got back `409 Conflict`. The task runner read that as a real pre-existing run, failed the parent task, and skipped the `trigger_run_id` XCom, even though the child run had been created.\n\nTwo changes:\n\n- The trigger POST now goes through `_request_without_retry`, so it is never automatically re-sent.\n- If the POST raises an ambiguous transport error (`httpx.ReadError`, `ReadTimeout`, `RemoteProtocolError`), the client probes `GET dag-runs/count` once for that run ID. If the run is there, the trigger is treated as successful, or cleared when `reset_dag_run=True`. If it is not there, the original error is re-raised.\n\n`ConnectError` and `PoolTimeout` mean the request never reached the server, so they propagate untouched with no probe. A direct `409` from the POST still returns `DAGRUN_ALREADY_EXISTS`, or clears with `reset_dag_run=True`, exactly as before.\n\n### Cost\n\nA trigger that succeeds costs one request, the same as before this PR. The probe only runs on a POST that already failed, so there is no extra round-trip on the hot path. `test_trigger` asserts the request list is exactly one POST, so this cannot regress silently.\n\nAn earlier revision of this PR did an unconditional `get_count` pre-check before every POST. That added a round-trip to every trigger, which @jason810496 pushed back on in https://github.com/apache/airflow/pull/66911#pullrequestreview-4410023505. The pre-check is gone.\n\n### Behaviour change\n\nWith the pre-check removed there is one case that differs from current `main`: if a Dag run genuinely already existed **and** the POST fails with an ambiguous transport error, the client returns `OKResponse` instead of `DAGRUN_ALREADY_EXISTS`, because it cannot tell that run apart from one its own lost POST created. That needs both a pre-existing run and a lost response in the same call. `reset_dag_run=True` is unaffected, that path still clears the run.\n\nDistinguishing the two would mean either the pre-check that was just removed, or comparing the found run's `logical_date`/`conf` against what was sent. I can add the latter if reviewers want the distinction back, but it did not seem worth the complexity for the case it covers.\n\ncloses: #66905\n\n### Tests\n\n- `pytest task-sdk/tests/task_sdk/api/test_client.py::TestDagRunOperations` (20 passed)\n- `pytest task-sdk/tests/task_sdk/api/test_client.py` (123 passed)\n- `prek run --files task-sdk/src/airflow/sdk/api/client.py task-sdk/tests/task_sdk/api/test_client.py`\n\n---\n\n##### Was generative AI tooling used to co-author this PR?\n\n- [X] Yes (please specify the tool below)\n\nGenerated-by: OpenAI Codex and Claude Code, following [the guidelines](https://github.com/apache/airflow/blob/main/contributing-docs/05_pull_requests.rst#gen-ai-assisted-contributions)\n\n---\n\n* Read the **[Pull Request Guidelines](https://github.com/apache/airflow/blob/main/contributing-docs/05_pull_requests.rst#pull-request-guidelines)** for more information. Note: commit author/co-author name and email in commits become permanently public when merged.\n* For fundamental code changes, an Airflow Improvement Proposal ([AIP](https://cwiki.apache.org/confluence/display/AIRFLOW/Airflow+Improvement+Proposals)) is needed.\n* When adding dependency, check compliance with the [ASF 3rd Party License Policy](https://www.apache.org/legal/resolved.html#category-x).\n* For significant user-facing changes create newsfragment: `{pr_number}.significant.rst`, in [airflow-core/newsfragments](https://github.com/apache/airflow/tree/main/airflow-core/newsfragments). You can add this file in a follow-up commit after the PR is created so you know the PR number.\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/airflow/issues/66911/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/airflow/issues/66911/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null}},"event":"cross-referenced"},{"id":32500232134,"node_id":"UNLE_lADOAgUK288AAAABQoAHTs8AAAAHkSovxg","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/airflow/issues/events/32500232134","actor":{"login":"pierrejeambrun","id":14861206,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0ODYxMjA2","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/14861206?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pierrejeambrun","html_url":"https://github.com/pierrejeambrun","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pierrejeambrun/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pierrejeambrun/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pierrejeambrun/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pierrejeambrun/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pierrejeambrun/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pierrejeambrun/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pierrejeambrun/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pierrejeambrun/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/use